    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Check LFTs b4 starting PO terbinafine (hepatotoxicity may occur ± liver dz). Periodic LFT monitoring = recommended; stop if liver inj develops."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Terbinafine inhibits CYP2D6:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " w TCAs, SSRIs, BBs, class 1C antiarrhythmics or MAO-B inhibitors, monitor carefully; the 2D6 drug may need a lower dose."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Ventricular dysfun:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ⍉for other indications unless the benefit clearly outweighs the risk. W CHF RF (ischemic or valvular Hdz, sig pulm dz such as COPD, renal failure or other edematous disorders), review risks and benefits, tx w caution and monitor for CHF; stop if signs or Sx of CHF appear. HF was reported more often @ a TDD of 400 mg, though also @ lower doses."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Boxed warning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " many CYP3A4 substrates are contraindicated w itraconazole, eg methadone, disopyramide, dofetilide, dronedarone, quinidine and ergot alkaloids."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Rare serious hepatotoxicity, some w.in the first wk: consider liver funct monitoring in all pts; stop @ once and test liver funct if signs of liver dysfun develop."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " QT-prolonging drugs met by CYP3A4, such as erythromycin, pimozide and quinidine."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Mod CYP2C9 and CYP3A4 inhibitor and strong CYP2C19 inhibitor: monitor narrow-therapeutic-window drugs met this way; the effect persists 4 to 5 days after stopping."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Rare serious hepatotoxicity, USU but ⍉always reversible on stopping: use w caution in liver dysfun; stop if signs of liver dz develop."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
